  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Gage Jump threw five scoreless innings and gave them everything they needed. The bats gave back nothing. That's how a team slides deeper into a streak.",
    "what_this_means": "Shutting out a lineup should earn at least one run in return. Instead they left runners scattered across eight innings. Eleven plate appearances with someone in scoring position and nothing to show. And watched the game get decided in the one inning when they couldn't manufacture even contact. Jump's line (five and two-thirds, five hits, one earned, seven strikeouts, 3.51 ERA) was good enough to win most games. Luis Medina and Hogan Harris kept it clean after him. The bullpen held. The offense did not. This is not a slump. This is a locked door, and they keep forgetting they have a key.",
